drm: h713-afbd: program proc integer phases when scaling

*** OUT OF patches/kernel/series SINCE 2026-09-23: SUPERSEDED BY THE VE SCALER.
***
*** This patch is one of six that let the display magnify a decoded picture
*** smaller than the panel (VE power-of-two scale-down to 960x544, then the
*** proc block at 0x05180000 back up to 1280x720). Patch 0120 replaced that
*** route: the VE's polyphase scaler produces arbitrary even sizes from 1x to
*** 4x per axis, so the decoder lands on exactly 1280x720 and the display has
*** nothing left to scale. The retired six are 0098, 0103, 0105, 0106, 0108
*** and 0111; they are a chain and only come back together.
***
*** Nothing in the shipping stack could still reach this path. mpv's vo_drm
*** refuses any configuration whose displayed source size differs from the
*** mode (patches/mpv/0003), and vd_lavc only ever asks the decoder to SHRINK
*** (patches/mpv/0004), so a sub-panel picture never reaches the plane at all.
***
*** REOPEN CONDITION: content SMALLER than the panel, magnified with no GPU --
*** 480p on this 720p panel. The VE cannot upscale, so that is the one job
*** this hardware block could still do. It would also need a producer that
*** writes the small picture into a panel-sized canvas (cedrus patch 0107
*** already separates COMPOSE from the capture canvas, so the kernel half
*** exists). Restore all six to `series` together; they were hardware-clean
*** when they were dropped, not broken.
***
*** See docs/handoff-2026-09-23-retire-display-scaling.md.
***
*** THIS ONE carries the integer-phase pair (H=3/V=2 for an upscale, H=4/V=3
*** at unity). Anyone reprogramming this block needs it; leaving the boot
*** firmware's unity values behind selects the wrong filter taps.
***

ProcWinNode::CalcWindow initializes the horizontal and vertical integer phase
fields to 3 and 2 for an upscale.  Unity is the exceptional case: its
fractional phases cross their thresholds, so the firmware advances the fields
to 4 and 3 and wraps the vertical fraction to zero.

The boot firmware leaves those unity values in 0x05180008.  Updating only the
fractional phases and ratios therefore selects the wrong filter taps while the
scaler is active.  Program all three fields together, following the firmware's
exact upscale path.

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/tiny/sun50i-h713-afbd.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/tiny/sun50i-h713-afbd.c
@@ -154,5 +154,9 @@
 #define PROC_BYPASS_BIT	BIT(27)
 #define PROC_RATIO_MASK		GENMASK(21, 0)
+#define PROC_H_INT_PHASE_MASK	GENMASK(30, 28)
+#define PROC_V_INT_PHASE_MASK	GENMASK(26, 24)
+#define PROC_H_INT_PHASE(v)	FIELD_PREP(PROC_H_INT_PHASE_MASK, (v))
+#define PROC_V_INT_PHASE(v)	FIELD_PREP(PROC_V_INT_PHASE_MASK, (v))
 #define PROC_PHASE_MASK		GENMASK(15, 0)
 #define PROC_FIELD16_MASK	GENMASK(15, 0)
 #define PROC_UNITY		0x10000u
@@ -393,8 +397,19 @@ static void h713_proc_configure(struct h713_afbd *h,
 	h713_proc_rmw(h, PROC_OUT_W_DUP, BIT(31) | PROC_FIELD16_MASK,
 		      BIT(31) | out_w);
 	h713_proc_rmw(h, PROC_FRAME_LINES, PROC_FIELD16_MASK,
 		      max(in_h, out_h));
-	h713_proc_rmw(h, PROC_RATIO_H, PROC_RATIO_MASK, ratio_h);
+	/*
+	 * ProcWinNode::CalcWindow starts the integer phases at H=3/V=2.
+	 * Unity is the exceptional case that advances each to H=4/V=3 while
+	 * wrapping the vertical fractional phase to zero.  The boot firmware
+	 * leaves those unity values behind, so retaining the upper fields while
+	 * changing only the fractions selects the wrong filter taps.
+	 */
+	h713_proc_rmw(h, PROC_RATIO_H,
+		      PROC_RATIO_MASK | PROC_H_INT_PHASE_MASK |
+		      PROC_V_INT_PHASE_MASK,
+		      ratio_h | PROC_H_INT_PHASE(3) |
+		      PROC_V_INT_PHASE(2));
 	h713_proc_rmw(h, PROC_RATIO_V, PROC_RATIO_MASK, ratio_v);
 	h713_proc_rmw(h, PROC_PHASE_H, PROC_PHASE_MASK,
 		      (PROC_UNITY + ratio_h) >> 2);
